WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.435
-The last time we talked was

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.437
Before "Avengers: Endgame"
came out.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.639
And that went on to be
the biggest movie

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.174
in the whole wide world ever.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.476
-Right, right, right, right.
-Yeah, giant.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:14.647
And then, I was reading
something about you

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.582
and about, you know,
"Black Panther."

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:19.619
And somewhere in the thing,
it said that you auditioned for

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.321
a different superhero
for Marvel at first.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:23.789
-I did. Drax, yeah, yeah.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.826
-You auditioned for Drax?
-Yeah, weirdly enough, yeah.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.961
-From "Guardians."
-From "Guardians."

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.797
-Let me just show everyone
who -- This is --

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.166
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.702
This is Drax.
-Batista.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.870
-Yeah, so you auditioned
for that?

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.572
-I did. I did.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.707
You know, it's about
going and playing.

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.409
I didn't think
I was gonna get it.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.945
And it's weird too, because it's
a testament, I think,

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.114
to Marvel because after each
film, you know --

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.183
"Ant-Man" has a different tone
and feeling.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.051
We didn't know
what that was gonna be.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.220
We didn't know what "Guardians"
was gonna be.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.555
So I didn't know what it was.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.523
And I only had
a few pages at that time.

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:59.425
So it was just good
to come in and play

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.793
to see what they did with it.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:03.028
-And they remembered you
from that and they go,

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:05.331
"Oh, we got to put him --
we have a role for him,

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.766
but we don't want to tell him"?

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.268
-Well, sometimes, that's the way
it works as an actor.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:11.270
You go in knowing
you're not gonna get it,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.406
but you're meeting the people
that, you know,

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.141
they might be like,
"He's not this,

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.043
but we'll put him in
this other thing."

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.879
So I feel like that was one of
the moments when they were like,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.247
"Hey, we could use him later."

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.149
-And I know
during the interview for --

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.550
-Sarah Finn, casting director.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.519
-Is that who did that?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.821
-I love giving shout-outs
to casting directors.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:31.257
-Sarah Finn, Sarah Finn.
-Sarah Finn, good job, Sarah.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.092
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.094
She did a great job, obviously.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.495
-Really worked well.

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:38.664
I loved your interviews that you
were doing during "Endgame"

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:40.733
because you had
to give interviews saying that

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.403
you were in the movie, but you
didn't want to spoil anything.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.371
That's the way it works with
Marvel movies.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.439
They don't really want you
to talk about much.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:48.807
Talk about, you know, they say,

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:51.244
"Watch, go see our movie,
but we can't spoil anything."

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.846
And you did something in your
interviews that made me laugh.

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.614
I think we showed it
on the show once.

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.750
But I want to show it to you
while you're here.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.252
Here's Chadwick Boseman not
spoiling "Avengers: Endgame."

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:01.454
Take a look at this.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.122
-People are, like, ready to see
this movie.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.624
They're buying the tickets.
It's nuts.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.025
I mean, how does
that feel to know

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.359
that they love this film
so much?

00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:09.028
-It's great, but I'm dead.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.263
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.464
So I can't answer any questions
about that.

00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:13.866
-Oh, okay.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.302
So you don't want to give us
a spoiler or anything like that?

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.370
-I'm dead.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.971
-What about "Black Panther 2"?
Anything?

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:19.905
-I'm dead.

00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:23.309
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh, man.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.478
-It made us laugh.
We showed it on the show.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.913
We loved it. It made me laugh.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.982
-It was the most fun
doing that, actually.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.115
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:31.684
-Where did you come up with,
"I'm dead"?

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:35.521
-Well, it was the first time
I had done press, you know,

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.189
in a minute since we shot it.

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:39.291
And so I was like,
"You know what?

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.793
I can make this real easy.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.262
I can just come out
and say, 'I'm dead.'"

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:44.330
It's that simple.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.699
-Because you did die or -- Yeah.

00:02:47.699 --> 00:02:51.637
-Yeah, and the funny thing about
it is, you coming in --

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.340
I didn't even know I was
gonna die that day.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.674
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:57.510
-Yeah, a lot of us, so today --

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.646
You don't have all the script
at times, you know,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.680
because of their secret,
secretive about stuff.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.716
-And you film all different
endings and stuff.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.518
-Yeah. Well, you have
different scripts.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.853
You have different scripts,
you know, like different --

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:08.788
to throw people off.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.989
-Wow. What are you gonna do?

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.858
Because you're filming
"Black Panther 2" now.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:12.992
You have all this time.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.561
You can't just tell everyone
you're dead.

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:18.264
-You know what?
I don't know what it is --

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.532
what it's gonna be this time,
but I'll come up with something.

00:03:20.532 --> 00:03:21.834
-Yeah, yeah, you are.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.103
-I got to do it tonight
before we do the premiere,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.938
because I'm on
the red carpet tonight.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:27.240
-Oh, that's right.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.941
-Yeah, you can be like,
"I'm back."

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.042
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.578
-"I'm back."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.946
-I want to talk about
"21 Bridges."

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.248
Congrats on this thing.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.416
-Thank you.

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:38.417
-How did you get involved with
this movie?

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:39.585
-Well, I was dead...

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:40.786
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:41.854
-This is unbelievable.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.355
-...after "Infinity War,"

00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:46.559
and the Russo brothers came to
me at the premiere after-party.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.794
-Did a great job, yeah.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.829
-Yeah, I think it was
a consolation.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.331
You're dead, so let me bring you
another movie.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:53.600
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.567
-And so, yeah, you know,
they were like,

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.670
"We think you're perfect for
this role."

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.838
And then I met Brian Kirk,
the director.

00:03:59.838 --> 00:04:02.608
I was like, "We're going to be
a great collaborator."

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.110
And we decided to produce it.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.846
-It's a good movie.
It's very -- I like the premise.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.147
There's a lot of action.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.216
But basically set it up
for everybody.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.318
The idea is --
-Eight cops are killed.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:17.723
I'm an NYPD detective
who's known for, you know,

00:04:17.723 --> 00:04:19.325
tracking down cop killers.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:22.194
And so I shut down
the city of Manhattan,

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:26.198
like, all of the entryways into
it, including the 21 bridges,

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:30.036
so that we can trap
the offenders and catch them.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.305
-They're stuck on --
-Stuck on the island.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.906
-Stuck on Manhattan.
-Yeah.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.340
-Yeah, you said 21 bridges.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.043
I didn't know there was
21 bridges around Manhattan.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:39.545
-I didn't either.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.181
Actually, when we started, the
script was called "17 Bridges."

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:45.784
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:48.387
No, they didn't build
four bridges but, you know,

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:51.257
I'm about to do
a speech about the 21 bridges.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.960
And I was like --
about the 17 bridges --

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.495
and they're like,
"We might have got it wrong.

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.331
We might have got it wrong."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.699
-Right, yeah. We got to recount.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.267
-They were gonna
rename the movie.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.435
"If we can't figure it out,

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.970
let's call the movie
'Lockdown.'"

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.270
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.572
-"Let's not even
mention bridges.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.673
We have to talk about bridges."

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.141
-I was like,
"Figure this out for me."

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.710
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. 21 bridges.

